// Immediate-form SFPCONFIG: (imm16, dest, mod1).  The mod mask 0xaa admits
// only {1,3,5,7} (write/OR/AND/XOR of Imm16, MOD1_IMM16_IS_VALUE set), so the
// instruction never reads LReg[0]; avoiding that register is its purpose.
// Lane-mask forms (mod1 bit 3) read LReg[0] (SFPCONFIG.md) and are excluded
// by the same mask.  Only dest 15 (LaneConfig) is accepted, checked in
// gimple-rvtt-check.cc (sfpconfig-imm-dest-unaudited): dests 0-8 belong to
// the macro planner, 9-10 are NonContractualBehavior, and 11-14 would change
// constant registers whose contents are not modelled.
RVTT_FN (sfpconfig_i,           ,,VOID_FTYPE_USI_USI_USI,                                    VOL, ({CU, 16}, {CU, 4}, {M, 0xaa}))
// SETC16 write, used to hoist a callee's address-modifier programming into
// its caller.  Args: SETC16 configuration register index, 16-bit value.
RVTT_FN (ttsetc16,              ,,VOID_FTYPE_USI_USI,                                        VOL, ({CU, 8}, {CU, 16}))
// All-lanes enable for hoisted initialization: expands to the all-lanes
// SFPENCC encoding that cc_enable_all_lanes_proved_p checks for.  No CC()
// flag: it is only inserted in a loop preheader at the outermost CC depth,
// and the expanded rvtt_sfpencc insn carries the CC effects at RTL.
RVTT_FN (sfpencc_all_lanes,     ,,VOID_FTYPE,                                                VOL, ())

